-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party notice: Hermes Agent
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository is an unofficial, community-maintained starter. It is not
affiliated with or endorsed by Nous Research.

It does not vendor Hermes Agent. `setup.sh` clones the upstream project at a
pinned commit from https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent, which is
copyright (c) Nous Research and its contributors and is likewise licensed under
the MIT License. Upstream's own LICENSE file is included in that checkout and
governs that code.

The file `patches/voice-and-desktop-features.patch` in this repository contains
MODIFICATIONS to Hermes Agent source files, distributed here as a diff rather
than as modified copies. Those modifications are the work of this repository's
contributors, are released under the MIT License above, and are applied to the
upstream checkout at install time. Applying the patch produces a modified
version of Hermes Agent; the upstream copyright notice continues to apply to
the unmodified portions.

The modifications add: Discord voice mixing, barge-in and join greetings,
background voice jobs, an on-demand local-CDP browser path, TTS runtime
overrides, optional streaming speech-to-text, and tests covering them.
